msgid "Some information does not live in posts: a phone number in the footer, opening hours in a theme option, event dates in custom fields. Use the <strong>Extra sources</strong> page to add it to the index:"
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>Fixed text:</strong> type any text (policies, FAQ, address). It is indexed as is."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>Part of a page:</strong> give a URL (on this site) and a CSS selector, such as <code>footer .contact</code> or <code>.soc-m h5</code>. Use \"Preview\" to check what will be read."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>WordPress options:</strong> names of WordPress options (wp_options table) whose values should be indexed. Put CSS selectors in the page field, not here."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>Custom fields:</strong> names of post meta fields (for example <code>_dateStart_event</code>) that are added to the text of each post when it is indexed."
msgstr ""

msgid "After any change, run the index again. The \"Indexed sources\" table on the Extra sources page shows what is in the index and warns about mistakes, such as a selector that matches nothing."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>Specific questions</strong> (\"what is the address?\"): the best passages are retrieved and the model writes the answer with citations."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>Lists and counts</strong> (\"list all products for pastures\", \"how many…\"): if the words match a category or tag, the chat uses all items of that term. A pure listing is answered directly by the plugin, with no model involved, so it is complete and consistent. The limit is \"Items for list questions\" in Settings → Answers."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>Dates:</strong> the model receives today's date, so \"next show\" works when the date is stored in a custom field that is indexed. Questions about a past year depend on the dates appearing in the indexed text."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>No answer:</strong> the chat says it did not find the information and shows no sources. Review these questions in History and add the missing content."
msgstr ""

msgid "Everything can be done from the terminal with WP-CLI, which is handy for large sites (no browser time limits) and for automation such as cron jobs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Command"
msgstr ""

msgid "Shows the key, models, number of indexed posts and chunks, and what is pending."
msgstr ""

msgid "Indexes new or changed content. Options: <code>--force</code> (re-index everything), <code>--post_type=product</code>, <code>--batch=20</code>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Indexes the Extra sources and prints warnings. Option: <code>--force</code>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Indexes a single post. Option: <code>--force</code>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Removes a post from the index."
msgstr ""

msgid "Empties the whole index (it can be rebuilt with <code>wp saic index</code>)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Shows the passages found for a query with their scores. Option: <code>--limit=20</code>. Great for debugging."
msgstr ""

msgid "Asks a question and prints the answer and sources, like a visitor would."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lists recent questions. Options: <code>--limit=50</code>, <code>--format=table|csv|json</code>."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>\"I did not find…\" but the content exists:</strong> run <code>wp saic search \"your question\"</code> (or check the Index page). If the page does not appear, it is not indexed: check the content types, re-index, or add it as an Extra source."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>Content changed but the answer is old:</strong> posts are re-indexed on save; for Extra sources, options and custom fields, run the index again."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>Lists are incomplete:</strong> raise \"Items for list questions\" and make sure the items belong to a category or tag that the question mentions."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>Empty answers or request errors:</strong> reasoning models need \"Max output tokens\" with room to spare; leave Temperature empty for them."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>The chat does not show:</strong> check that the floating button is enabled (or the block/shortcode is on the page), that \"Home page only\" is not limiting it, and clear any page cache."
msgstr ""

